#3007
The Dining Hall~
   A loaf of bread sits on the table, an empty waterskin hangs from a
hook, and a stone fountain bubbles quietly in the corner. 'get bread'
and then 'eat bread' takes care of hunger - you cannot eat food you are
not holding. 'get waterskin', 'fill waterskin from fountain' and 'drink
waterskin' (or just 'drink fountain') take care of thirst.
~
